Ray Dataset / Webdataset / MosaicML dataset (mds)\
\
Caching pattern:\
## The general caching strategies across ALL frameworks\
\
Strategy 1 \'97 Load into RAM upfront:\
  works when: dataset fits in RAM\
  how: load everything before training loop\
  frameworks: PyTorch TensorDataset, numpy arrays\
  
\f4 \uc0\u8592 
\f1  simplest! just load it all\
\
Strategy 2 \'97 Framework cache operator:\
  works when: dataset too big for RAM initially\
              but fits after first pass\
  how: .cache() or .materialize()  \
	e.g. TF: dataset = tf.data.Dataset.from_tensor_slices((X, y))\
					
\f0\b .cache()
\f1\b0  # 
\f4 \uc0\u8592 
\f1  explicit! caches in RAM after first \
		Ray: ds = ray.data.read_parquet("s3://my-bucket/data/") \
			# pin in Ray object store (shared memory across workers)\
			
\f0\b ds = ds.materialize()
\f1\b0 \
  frameworks: TensorFlow, Ray\
  
\f4 \uc0\u8592 
\f1  automatic! framework handles it\
\
Strategy 3 \'97 Local disk cache:\
  works when: dataset on remote storage (S3, GCS)\
              too big for RAM\
  how: download to local SSD first\
  frameworks: WebDataset cache_dir, manual rsync\
  
\f4 \uc0\u8592 
\f1  SSD >> network speed\
  
\f4 \uc0\u8592 
\f1  download once, train many epochs\
\
Strategy 4 \'97 Shared memory / object store:\
  works when: multiple workers need same data\
  how: Ray object store, mmap files\
  frameworks: Ray .materialize()\
  
\f4 \uc0\u8592 
\f1  one copy shared across all workers\
  
\f4 \uc0\u8592 
\f1  no duplication!\
\
Strategy 5 \'97 Prefetch only (no caching):\
  works when: dataset too big for any cache\
  how: async prefetch next batch while GPU trains\
  frameworks: all! (DataLoader num_workers, .prefetch())\
  
\f4 \uc0\u8592 
\f1  doesn't cache but hides I/O latency\
  
\f4 \uc0\u8592 
\f1  minimum viable optimization\
\
\
