\f0\b \cf0 Data ingestion flow
\f1\b0 \
Binary file (on SSD)\
    
\f4 \uc0\u8595 
\f1  read bytes\
In-memory array (NumPy)\
  shape: (60000, 28, 28) uint8\
    
\f4 \uc0\u8595 
\f1  convert\
tf.Tensor / torch.Tensor\
  shape: (60000, 28, 28) float32\
  
\f0\b normalized
\f1\b0 : divide by 255  -> 
\f5 \'ce\'aa\'ca\'b2\'c3\'b4\'d2\'aa
\f1 normalize : these values flow through matrix multiplications must be small or gradients explode!\
  so values become 0.0 to 1.0\
    
\f4 \uc0\u8595 
\f1  batch\
Mini-batch tensor\
  shape: (32, 28, 28)  
\f4 \uc0\u8592 
\f1  32 images at a time\
    
\f4 \uc0\u8595 
\f1  flatten for simple model\
  shape: (32, 784)     
\f4 \uc0\u8592 
\f1  28\'d728=784 pixels per image\
    
\f4 \uc0\u8595 
\f1  feed into model\
Forward pass!\
\
Labels: only used for Loss calculation\
\
Raw format -> numpy (on CPU ) -> tensor (in GPU) -> forward passing\
**MOST IMPORTANT** NumPy has no autograd, it doenst remember intermediate computation result, so it can\'92t do backprop, but tensor remembers it\
\

\f0\b *[optional] Data ingestion flow thru GDS\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf0 Raw format -> GPU (VRAM) -> forward passing\
With NVIDIA GDS support ( cuFile API ) \
\
\
\
\
Chain law for backprop \
FORWARD:\
x 
\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  (\'d7W1+b1) 
\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  z 
\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  (ReLU) 
\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  a 
\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  (\'d7W2+b2) 
\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  loss\
\
BACKWARD (chain rule):\
d(loss)/d(W1) = d(loss)/d(a) \'d7 d(a)/d(z) \'d7 d(z)/d(W1)\
                	  \uc0\u9492 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9496    \u9492 \u9472 \u9472 \u9496      \u9492 \u9472 \u9472 \u9496 \
               		    gradient from    ReLU          linear layer\
                	     next layer       derivative    derivative\
                                		     (1 or 0!)        (= input x)\
\
\
