\f0\b \cf0 CPU vs GPU:
\f1\b0 \
CPU:\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f4 \cf0 \uc0\u10003 
\f1  running your operating system\
  
\f4 \uc0\u10003 
\f1  loading files\
  
\f4 \uc0\u10003 
\f1  complex logic and branching\
  
\f4 \uc0\u10003 
\f1  general purpose anything\
  
\f7 \uc0\u10007 
\f1  doing 10,000 simple things simultaneously\
GPU:\

\f4 \uc0\u10003 
\f1  matrix multiplication (exactly what ML needs!)\
  
\f4 \uc0\u10003 
\f1  doing same operation on millions of numbers\
  
\f4 \uc0\u10003 
\f1  parallel computation\
  
\f7 \uc0\u10007 
\f1  complex logic\
  
\f7 \uc0\u10007 
\f1  general purpose tasks\
Forward pass = multiply input matrix by weight matrices\
             = billions of simple multiplications\
             = PERFECT for GPU!\
\
CPU doing this:  8 cores  \'d7 sequential = slow\
GPU doing this:  8000 cores \'d7 parallel  = fast!\
\
Training speedup: GPU can be 100x faster than CPU for ML!\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
