\f0\b \cf0 RAM vs VRAM 
\f8 \'c4\'da\'b4\'e6
\f0  vs 
\f8 \'cf\'d4\'b4\'e6
\f1\b0 \
RAM (System Memory):\
  attached to CPU\
  your laptop might have 16-32GB\
  stores: OS, applications, files you're working on\
\
VRAM (Video RAM):\
  attached to GPU\
  consumer GPU: 8-24GB\
  pro GPU (A100)
\f0\b : 40-80GB
\f1\b0 \
  stores: model weights, gradients, training data batches\
\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f9\i\b \cf0 KEY RULE:
\f1\i0\b0 \
  
\f0\b CPU can only work with RAM\
  GPU can only work with VRAM\
  they CANNOT directly access each other's memory!
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 PCIe
\f1\b0  \'97 the highway between 
\f0\b CPU and GPU
\f1\b0 \
= the physical connection slot/bus between CPU and GPU on motherboard\
Think of it as a highway: \
CPU land 
\f4 \uc0\u8592 
\f1 \uc0\u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472  PCIe highway \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 \u9472 
\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  GPU land \
(RAM) 			   (data travels) 			(VRAM)\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 PCIe 4.0 (common today): ~32 GB/s \
PCIe 5.0 (newer): ~64 GB/s \
Sounds fast but remember: \
	VRAM internal speed: 2000 GB/s \
	PCIe between CPU-GPU: 32 GB/s \
	PCIe is 60x SLOWER than VRAM! 
\f4 \uc0\u8592 
\f1  this is a bottleneck!\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
\cf0 NVLlink:  connects GPU and GPU\
Multiple GPUs in one machine: \
Without NVLink (using PCIe): \
	GPU1 
\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  CPU 
\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  GPU2 
\f4 \uc0\u8592 
\f1  must go through CPU! \
	speed: ~32 GB/s  * CPU(or PCIe) becomes middleman bottleneck \
With NVLink:  (only on high end GPUs A100 H100)\
	GPU1 
\f4 \uc0\u8592 
\f1 \uc0\u9472 \u9472 NVLink\u9472 \u9472 
\f4 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  GPU2 
\f4 \uc0\u8592 
\f1  direct connection! \
	speed: ~600 GB/s 18x faster than PCIe!\
	CPU completely bypassed\
GPU / GPU exchanges things like gradients after each iterations\
